.TH SYSINFO 1 "August 2026" "sysinfo 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysinfo \- print a concise Linux system information summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysinfo
.RB [ \-p | \-\-public-ip ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysinfo
prints the current system load, root filesystem usage, memory and swap use,
process count, established SSH connection count, non-link-local network
addresses, and system uptime.
.PP
It is an independent POSIX shell utility with an output style inspired by
landscape-sysinfo. It neither requires nor communicates with Landscape.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-public-ip
Also query the local cloud metadata service at 169.254.169.254 for a public
IPv4 address. This is useful when the provider maps a public address to a
private interface address using NAT. No metadata request is made by default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/loadavg
Current load average.
.TP
.I /proc/meminfo
Memory statistics.
.TP
.I /proc/uptime
System uptime.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after printing the summary.
.SH AUTHOR
Jacek Stypuła.
